# candidate T22 Change 8 -- STREAMED decomposition (a WALL removal)
#   commit::commit_streamed decomposes one block at a time and drops it,
#   so the 68.7 GiB Decomp.message is never built; quadeval::
#   honest_z_from_raw rebuilds one block's s per iteration in the second
#   pass; quadeval::carrier_from_raw needs no decomposition at all,
#   because carrier_entry's gadget_mul cancels against it.
# This run is a GUARD, not a speed claim. Change 8 only ADDS functions:
#   every row measured here is code that is byte-identical in both arms,
#   so the question it answers is whether adding the items perturbed the
#   codegen of the ones that were there. Nothing may read slower.
# The streamed items' own rows are registered AFTER this run: a new row
#   needs the item in the  crate too, so it cannot be A/B'd.
# Measured peak RSS (VmHWM, in-process): materialized grows 72.5 MiB per
#   block, streamed 8 MiB per block (the raw input alone) -- 774 vs 324
#   MiB at 8 blocks. At BLOCKS = 1024 that is ~74 GiB against ~8.5 GiB.
